# Line endings: Terraform configuration, templates and shell scripts are always checked out with LF,
# on every platform. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout would otherwise turn them into CRLF,
# and Terraform then renders CRLF into values such as EC2 user_data — a CRLF-only difference against
# infrastructure applied from Linux (observed on the production Tailscale router launch template).
# The repository already stores these files with LF, so these rules change no file content.
*.tf     text eol=lf
*.tftpl  text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
